{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>They saw the voices.</b> As in וְלִבִּי רָאָה (Ecclesiastes 1:16). They perceived the nature of the voices — that they could not endure them, as they said: לֹא אֹסִיף עוֹד לִשְׁמֹעַ אֶת קוֹל יהוה אֱלֹהַי, וְאֶת הָאֵשׁ הַגְּדוֹלָה הַזֹּאת לֹא אֶרְאֶה עוֹד, וְלֹא אָמוּת (Deuteronomy 18:16)." "<b>And the people saw.</b> They considered what to do." "<b>And they trembled.</b> One who sways with an undirected movement toward some boundary is called נע, as in וַיְנִיעֵם בַּמִּדְבָּר (Numbers 32:13), תָּנוּעַ אֶרֶץ כַּשִּׁכּוֹר (Isaiah 24:20). This is because out of their fear they recoiled backward from some boundary they were at, undirected toward any boundary beyond it."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:26:34.322306043Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}